RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     In a locale where langinfo data is not defined, nnll__llaannggiinnffoo() returns a
     pointer to the corresponding string in the POSIX locale.  nnll__llaannggiinnffoo__ll()
     returns the same values as nnll__llaannggiinnffoo().  In all locales, nnll__llaannggiinnffoo()
     returns a pointer to an empty string if _i_t_e_m contains an invalid setting.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     For example:

           nl_langinfo(ABDAY_1)

     would return a pointer to the string "Dom" if the identified language was
     Portuguese, and "Sun" if the identified language was English.

